            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative study of coronary artery disease using Fourier analysis in radionuclide ventriculography and coronary arteriography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>166-8, 190-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of rest blood-equilibrium radionuclide ventriculography (RVG) and of coronary arteriography were reviewed together. In 12 angiographically proved CAD patients, Fourier analysis correctly diagnosed 11, with an accuracy of 83.33% in localization 9 patients with myocardial infarction showed &quot;empty&quot; area in phase images. The phase analysis in RVG was considered a sensitive and accurate method in evaluating patients of CAD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
